Search for "QN-Java project file" key phrase to find every file created for QN-Java.

Cheatsheet for cognitive modelling:
Do not use "nil" in strings that you send to the model
empty strings "" will fail, not in the model but in the Java code that handles the model.
strings must also be lower case.

For modifying the imaginal buffer, use =imaginal> in the RHS of a production, +imaginal> will replace the chunk
entirely.
forbidden names:
{"nil", "error", "busy", "free", "empty", "full", "lowest", "highest", "current"}

in a customized manual action, always send at least para-1 and para-2.

Need to be careful there seems to be a problem with ?aural> state free
because evaluating it on the LHS doesn't prevent from attending a new sound
while the previous was not yet recoded.

ingescape bug when the platform is on another computer, the callback are not registered except if line 16789 of function.java
is uncommented...

There is no implementation of the modification request to the imaginal buffer *imaginal> which means
that only =imaginal> can be used but it is not taking into account process time and workload.

How to model low-workload situations, for instance I need to detect a new task (thus a new label
on the interface) and my solution right now is to have a continuous visual polling of the label which
loads the visual and imaginal modules, but I think the model should not continuously read, I am tempted
to use the temporal module, but I prefer to ask the question beforehand.